{"type":"text","text":"Done — all three addresses found, proven, recorded, and promoted into the ROM's shared mapping file.\n\n## Results\n\n| Variable | Address | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| Link X (horizontal) | **`$0070`** | 1 byte, direct screen pixel, 0 = left edge, increases rightward |\n| Link Y (vertical) | **`$0084`** | 1 byte, direct screen pixel, 0 = top, increases downward |\n| Current map location | **`$00EB`** | overworld screen index `row*16 + col` = `(row<<4)|col`; north −16, south +16, east +1, west −1 |\n\n(The bridge was already on the first overworld screen with Link alive, so the title-screen navigation wasn't needed.)\n\n## How each was found and proven\n\n**`$0070` (X).** Differential search: snapshot → hold Right 30 frames → snapshot gave 30 \"increased\" survivors (all zero-page/stack noise), with `$0070` = 120→160. Left 30 reverseed it to 119, Right again back to 160. `$0070`, `$0000` and OAM-shadow `$024B`/`$024F` moved together.\n*Proof:* saved state, wrote 60 to `$0070` while paused, stepped 2 frames → screenshot showed Link teleported from the center to the **left path (x≈56)**; the game then held 56. Writing `$0084` in the same session moved him only vertically, confirming the split.\n\n**`$0084` (Y).** Snapshot → hold Down 30 → snapshot gave 31 \"increased\" survivors including `$0084` = 141→181 (+40).\n*Proof:* loaded the saved state, wrote 40 to `$0084` while paused, stepped 2 frames → screenshot showed Link teleported **straight up to the top edge (y≈45, x unchanged at ≈160)**, value settling to 45.\n\n**`$00EB` (map).** Snapshotted on the start screen (`0x77`), walked north one screen (`0x67`, rock screen), walked back south (`0x77`). Of 132 \"changed\" addresses, only `$00EB` (with its shadow) returned exactly across the round trip; `0x77`→`0x67` is exactly −16 = one row north.\n*Proof:* wrote `$00EB = 0x67` while the start screen was still displayed (the byte stuck at 103, the room stayed drawn — the loader only runs at a transition), then held Up 170 frames. The transition computed from the written value: Link landed on a **third, distinct screen** (0x57, row 5 col 7) and `$00EB`/`$00EC` became 87. Repeating while writing **only** `$00EB` (leaving `$00EC = 0x77`) gave the same third screen and `0x57`, so `$00EB` is authoritative and **`$00EC` is a copy synced at room load**.\n\nRecorded all three (`mapping_type: address`, source `differential search`) and called `promote_mappings` — the file now holds 3 addresses. The game is restored to the saved start-screen state and running."}
